In the figure, triangle ABC is inscribed in circle O, CD is perpendicular to AB at point P, intersecting circle O at point D, and E is the midpoint of AC. Line EP intersects BD at point F, and the diameter of circle O is d. The following conclusions are given: 
1. EF is perpendicular to BD; 
2. The value of AC² + BD² is a constant; 
3. OE = (1/2)BD; 
4. AB • CD = 2S<sub>quadrilateral ADBC</sub>. 
How many of the above statements are correct? ( )
A. 1
B. 2
C. 3
D. 4

As shown in the figure, if the rectangular paper is folded along the dashed line ① and then cut along the dashed line ② to create a right triangle, the unfolded triangle will be an isosceles triangle. The perimeter of the unfolded triangle is ( )
A. 6 + 2 \sqrt{5}
B. 6 + 4 \sqrt{5}
C. 4 + 2 \sqrt{5}
D. 4 + 4 \sqrt{5}

Given the three views of a certain geometric body (unit: cm) as shown in the figure, what is the volume of this geometric body?
A. 100 cm^{3}
B. 98 cm^{3}
C. 88 cm^{3}
D. 78 cm^{3}

In the figure, in the quadrangular prism ABCD-A₁B₁C₁D₁, the base ABCD is a square with a side length of 3, the length of the lateral edge AA₁ is 4, and the angles between AA₁ and A₁B₁, A₁D₁ are both 60°. What is the length of AC₁?
A. 10
B. \sqrt{56}
C. \sqrt{10}
D. \sqrt{34}

If Xiao Qiang randomly throws a dart at the square wooden board shown in Figure 5, what is the probability that the dart lands in the shaded area? (Examining probability)
A. \frac{1}{6}
B. \frac{1}{8}
C. \frac{1}{9}
D. \frac{1}{12}

